  "source_review": {
    "revision": "5fcd8a81e7b024abdf6a50d2c3d3d566da71dd8f",
    "findings": [],
    "invariants": [
      "Only aligned side-16 masks accepted by the existing exact_patch_halo check enter the index. Profile, seed, min_y, height and all generator float bits remain in CacheKey.",
      "Normal 2048 chunk-key insertion/order and 8192 column cache limits are unchanged. New entries do not bypass generation checks or fallback: they only supplement the already-optional job snapshot.",
      "Snapshot filtering retains the original nearby neighborhood and excludes tiles covered by initial terrain. The snapshot neither mutates the index nor refreshes recency.",
      "Actual tile publication refreshes recency. Existing full-key values remain immutable, and snapshots own Arcs independently of index/alias eviction.",
      "At most 24 map/deque entries and 256 MiB of conservatively counted backing allocation capacity per engine. Shared buffers can be overcounted. In-flight jobs can retain their own references after cache eviction; this is not a claim that total process RSS is 256 MiB.",
      "Ineligible or oversized tiles use the unchanged normal cache and generation path. No expanded mask/metadata domains, different guards, RNG, feature ordering or fallback coverage.",
      "Default CaveCache destruction/reset drops the additional index too. There is no per-profile map or unbounded retention outside engine ownership.",
      "The 48-entry experiment is preserved on codex/nether-held-resident48; selected HEAD native tree exactly matches the originally built 24-entry candidate."
    ],
    "tradeoffs": [
      "More bounded memory is retained in exchange for avoiding repeated exact GPU work. Generation RSS, actual hits/tiles, full outputs and later sustained/concurrent runs must decide acceptance.",
      "Direct terrain_field queries retain their current lookup; this prototype improves the existing job snapshot path only."
    ],
